{
  "_what": "Vital Plant Living, a plant-based kitchen on the street: a builder for your own bowl or wrap, a menu of named combos from around the world, a counter, and a stereo. tools/make-vital.py builds every generated part of vital-plant-living.html and the room's credits in liner-notes.html from this file. Do not hand-edit between the markers.",
  "_pantry": "THE PANTRY IS RYAN'S OWN, the list he cooks from for himself, given in his brief for this room on 2026-09-24. It is written down as he gave it -- his section names, his words, his capitals, 'Herbs de Provence' and 'Babaganoush' included -- with three kinds of change and no others: (1) a line that held several things is split into its things, because a builder needs something to tick: 'Beans: black, pinto, garbanzo' is three beans and 'Curry paste: red, green' is two pastes; (2) 'Rice' is Basmati rice, Jasmine rice and Sushi rice, Ryan's correction the same morning, and 'Basmatic' in that message is read as the typo it is; (3) a thing on the list twice is in the builder once, in the first section it appears in -- bell peppers are on the list three times and are under Base/Filling. The trinities' own ingredients are NOT in the pantry and are not added to it: 'lemon grass' belongs to the Thai base Ryan wrote down, and choosing that base brings it. The supplements at the foot of Ryan's list are not on this menu at all, because this street gives no advice about eating (Samefood Cafe's rule) and a restaurant serving B12 would be giving some.",
  "_looks": "Every item in the builder has a look -- a shape and an ink -- so the section of your bowl can draw it. make-vital.py refuses an item with no look, because the failure is not an error anywhere: it is a thing you ticked that never appears in the picture, which reads as broken. The inks are the room's food inks in love.css, all ornament, all carried by an --vpl-ink outline.",
  "_combos": "THE COMBOS ARE OURS, written for this room, and every one of them is assembled out of the pantry above and stands on one or more of the flavour bases Ryan wrote down. make-vital.py refuses an item that is not in the pantry, a base that is not in his list, and a combo with no base at all -- so a combo cannot quietly bring in an ingredient the kitchen does not keep. Where the dish a combo is thinking about is usually made with something the pantry does not have, the note says so rather than pretending: red beans and rice uses kidney beans, and this pantry has pinto. Nothing on this menu is called authentic, exotic or ethnic, and the tool refuses all three in our voice: a bowl somebody builds themselves out of one person's pantry is not a claim about anybody's grandmother's cooking.",
  "_ital": "THE NAME IS A TRANSLATION AND THE ROOM SAYS SO. Ryan's brief called the room Ital Plant Livity, and Ital and livity are Rastafari words: Ital from 'vital', with its first syllable replaced by the I of I and I, and livity for the way of life it belongs to. Ryan's call, 2026-09-24: Rastafari has been a big influence on him, and the room takes a more general name. Two reasons, and both are in the room's own copy: this kitchen uses salt, MSG, soy sauce and processed food, which many people who keep Ital do not, so calling the menu Ital would be making a claim about it that is false in Rastafari's own terms; and practice varies among Rastafari, which is not ours to settle from outside. So the menu never calls a dish Ital, and make-vital.py refuses the word in any combo and in the counter. The stereo is the one place it stays, because it is in the songs' own titles and they are the musicians' to name.",
  "_checked": "2026-09-24",
