  "playlist": {
    "id": "PLZ6xBLBiTfpc",
    "title": "Ital Plant Livity",
    "channel": "Stimpunks Foundation",
    "_read": "Read off the playlist page's own data (ytInitialData) on 2026-09-24. The header says nineteen videos and eighteen render, with YouTube's 'Show unavailable videos' offered, so one entry is hidden from everybody but the playlist's owner; YouTube skips it. Every one of the eighteen was checked on its own watch page the same day: playabilityStatus OK and playableInEmbed true for all of them. The first visible entry is NgcI47HPM9A, which plays; the Queercore deck on the dancefloor failed to embed because of a dead video at the top of its list, so the hidden entry's position matters, and the embed was pressed inside a frame on the dev server before this room shipped rather than taken on trust -- which is how it was found not to play at all. See door_why.",
    "_order": "The playlist's own order, which is Ryan's, and is not re-sorted here. No random start: this is a running order somebody chose, the Chappell's reason.",
    "_drift": "The list under the stereo is a MIRROR of the playlist and drifts by design. A song added to the playlist plays the next time somebody puts the stereo on and is not listed here until somebody reads the playlist again and adds a row. The room prints the date this file was read. If a row dies, check-jukebox.py is what notices.",
    "frame": "door",
    "door_why": "Measured 2026-09-24, framed from a page on the dev server so the referrer was real: every frame of this playlist -- videoseries and listType forms, on youtube-nocookie.com and on youtube.com, and a frame started at a song on it that plays -- shows YouTube's 'This video is unavailable', while every song on it plays in a frame of its own and the Laughingstock playlist, framed the same way beside it, plays. So the fault is the playlist and not the songs or this site, and nothing in this repo can fix it. The likeliest cause is the entry YouTube hides as unavailable, but that is a guess and the page does not say it. Until it is sorted out on YouTube the whole playlist is a DOOR and not a screen -- a link out, shaped like one -- and each song is its own press. When it is fixed: press play inside a frame (not the poster), then set frame to 'screen' and re-run make-vital.py. Ryan's diagnosis the same day: 'allow embedding' was switched off on the playlist itself, a setting on the list that playableInEmbed on each video cannot see. He switched it on and it kept resetting to off, so the door stands."
  },
